        "thinking": "I'm working through the derivation of रौडृँ in भ्वादि with अनादरे sense, applying यङ् and णिच् with लुङ् to get the कर्तरि परस्मैपद उत्तम पुरुष एकवचन form with the प्र prefix, carefully tracking the reduplication and guṇa/vṛddhi changes to the root.\n\nNow I'm applying यस्य हलः to delete य of यङ् before the णिच् suffix, checking whether नाग्लोपिशास्वृदिताम् blocks the उपधा ह्रस्व since रौडृँ is ऋदित्, and working through whether that ऋदित्त्व still applies once यङ् has intervened.\n\nI'm tracing through बोभूय+णिच् in लुङ्चङ् to see if reduplication applies again beyond the existing अभ्यास, since 6.1.8's अनभ्यासस्य restricts चङ् reduplication to the non-reduplicated portion of the root — so I need to figure out which part counts as the \"first ekāc\" for यङन्त stems.\n\nBuilding on that, for उत्तमपुरुष एकवचन I'm applying णेरनिटि to delete णि, then using तान्तन्तामः to get मिप्→अम्, giving अरोरौडम् with pararūpa sandhi and finally प्ररोरौडम् with प्र-, while also checking whether णत्व applies here.\n\nRechecking the sandhi, I realize प्र + अरोरौडम् actually undergoes सवर्णदीर्घ to give प्रारोरौडम्. I also verify that यङ् is valid for this root since it's an एकाच् हलादि root, and confirm the अभ्यास formation रौड् → रो through ह्रस्व and गुण rules for यङ्लुक्, yielding रोरौड्यते correctly.\n\nNow moving to the second question, I'm examining the root घुट् (प्रतिघाते) listed in तुदादि गण, specifically whether it belongs to the कुटादि subgroup governed by गाङ्कुटादिभ्योऽञ्णिन्ङित् — checking other members like कुट, पुट, कुच, गुज to place it properly.\n\nI'm also checking घुट्'s kuṭādi status and whether that ṅittva actually affects anything here — since yaṅ is already ṅit, ṇic takes its own it-marker, and san following ṇic wouldn't be governed by the kuṭādi rule anyway since that rule applies to san directly after the root, not after ṇic.\n\nWorking through yaṅ-pratyaya on घुट्: applying reduplication rules (halādiḥ śeṣaḥ, kuhoś cuḥ, abhyāse cara, guṇa